            <ArticleTitle>Atypical Facial Filler Granuloma: Comparative Histologic Analysis with Paraffinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>169-172</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7181/acfs.2016.17.3.169</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dermal fillers are generally accepted as safe and well-tolerable cosmetic tools. However, adverse reactions have been reported in the literature. Here, we present a case of atypical facial filler granuloma and compare its histologic features with those of the classic paraffinoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
